			<div class="content" id="post-content-2791933">
									

<blockquote>
<p>It's quite long for a relatively simple idea already.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'd suggest that this one's a simple idea that gets more interesting and complex with additional exploration.</p>
<p>I'm an upvote myself as it stands, but I wouldn't mind seeing this expanded: that Elton idea has some twisted potential, methinks. Do want to know what happens if someone wears more than one mask, or an already transformed person wears a second (or third, or fourth, or fifth&#8230;) mask like Roget suggested, too- if nothing else its the sort of &quot;poke it to see what it does&quot; experiment the Foundation can't resist, and an excuse to go off on some weird tangents: Say, a hybrid ends up being uniquely well suited to the park's ecosystem and starts acting like an invasive species until they put it down, or finds an unfilled niche in the ecosystem.</p>
<p>You could also leave the number of locations ambiguous. Keep the list, just change the preceding sentence to not give an exact number, something like &quot;major attractions include:&quot;. That would give you more room to play with minor attractions (say, a couple platypi associated with a fountain, that sort of thing) or for there to suddenly be a boat ride because you need a large pond for your crocodiles.</p>

							</div>

								
