					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tl333s" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1304786); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1304786&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609448845" alt="TL333s" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1304786)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tl333s" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1304786); return false;" >TL333s</a></span> <span class="odate time_1492210940 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Apr 2017 23:02</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2792153">
									

<p>I dunno, I was all set for an anomalous amusement park, but this didn't really do anything for me. Maybe it's the nagging sense of wondering why someone would make this. I mean, your options when you enter are A) get attacked by animal people, or B) become one yourself, and rather quickly. Not exactly fun for the whole family. A couple notes:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Outside of testing, no personnel should enter SCP-2479's active zone at any time without permission from Site Director ██████.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This belongs in the containment procedures. I'd put it at the end of the first paragraph, myself.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a primitive scratching and biting manner</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Tone. I'm not sure what makes this 'primitive' or differentiates it from other forms of the same act, to illustrate.</p>

							</div>

								
					
