															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/haydenhead" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3057100); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3057100&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609448845" alt="Haydenhead" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3057100)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/haydenhead" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3057100); return false;" >Haydenhead</a></span> <span class="odate time_1492245123 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Apr 2017 08:32</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2792436">
									

<p>Thanks for the advice.</p>
<p>I've moved the first quotation to the Special Containment Procedures section, thank you for pointing that out.</p>
<p>I thought about your first point and realised the contradictory nature of having a park filled with &quot;mascots&quot; that are violent towards guests for no apparent reason, and so have rewritten the third of the aggressive reaction criteria list. Thanks for the idea, and for instigating me to rewrite it: you were right, it was unnecessary.</p>
<p>&quot;Primitive&quot; was the second word I chose, after &quot;animalistic&quot;.<br />
I wanted to choose my words carefully to suggest that -A are bestial, but maintain basic human characteristics even after affliction. &quot;Primitive&quot; simply sounds more human, which I thought was in my best interests to preserve in an article with a strong human body horror element.</p>

