					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/malvastor" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5704875); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5704875&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609448845" alt="Malvastor" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5704875)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/malvastor" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5704875); return false;" >Malvastor</a></span> <span class="odate time_1572269660 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Oct 2019 13:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4408705">
									

<p>The basic premise is alright, but I <em>absolutely</em> don't understand why the Foundation would go full mad scientist and decide to &quot;breed&quot; an instance that's even more dangerous and difficult to contain. The bits about it being a superpredator to keep the population down don't make a lot of sense if the things were already preying on each other. And if even if they weren't, why can't the population be kept down by ordinary culling?</p>
<p>The result is that when the -AX escapes and mates with the female instances, the intended &quot;oh crap&quot; feeling is lost under a &quot;what were they <em>thinking</em>!?&quot;</p>

							</div>

								
					
